/*
# Add electronics catalog products

1. New products
- Adds 20 electronics products to the existing `products` catalog.
- Each product includes the requested name, price, SKU, category, approved subcategory, description, stock, and four product image URLs.

2. Modified data
- Uses the existing `products` table with `category = 'electronics'`.
- Keeps existing products unchanged.
- Uses deterministic slugs and SKUs so this migration can be safely re-run.

3. Security
- No tables, permissions, or row-level security policies are changed.
- Product rows remain governed by the existing `products` table policies.

4. Important notes
- Image URLs point to relevant stock photography selected for product context; they are not copied Amazon listing photos.
- Existing rows with the same slugs are updated rather than duplicated.
*/

ON CONFLICT (slug) DO UPDATE SET name = EXCLUDED.name, category = EXCLUDED.category, subcategory = EXCLUDED.subcategory, short_description = EXCLUDED.short_description, description = EXCLUDED.description, price = EXCLUDED.price, sku = EXCLUDED.sku, sizes = EXCLUDED.sizes, colors = EXCLUDED.colors, images = EXCLUDED.images, stock = EXCLUDED.stock, status = EXCLUDED.status, audience = EXCLUDED.audience, is_new = EXCLUDED.is_new, is_featured = EXCLUDED.is_featured, is_best_seller = EXCLUDED.is_best_seller;
